{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-tirewear-default-db-fixture",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7c': `process-tirewear` computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE. It mounts `moves-onroad.esm`, which carries the 38 default-database tables and the logic, and supplies the eleven things that are this fixture's: ten runspec selections -- year 2020, August, hour 7, weekdays, source type 21, road type 4, its four source-fuel types, three pollutant-processes, the chained-to pair, and county 26161 -- and the expected output.\n\nTHE RUNSPEC IS THE CONFIGURATION, which is the whole point of the split: `spikes/7c/tirewear_fixture.esm` is 12 lines because the catalogue it mounts is a snapshot of ONE run and has nothing left to configure. This document is longer because the thing it mounts is national, and every line of the difference is a selection somebody made rather than a table somebody copied.\n\nWHY THE SELECTIONS ARE PARQUET and not written here as numbers: the logic ingests them (`update.kind: \"data\"`), which is what sizes the axes they are the extent of, and an ingesting document holds exactly one model (F45) -- so there is nowhere here to put an equation that would state them inline. They are read from the same snapshot the oracle comes from, which is where this run's runspec is written down.\n\n`tw_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in the snapshot catalogue: reading it would transcribe the answer. run-tests.sh compares against it from outside.\n\nIT EMITS THE SAME 375 ROWS as `fixtures/process-tirewear.esm` and `spikes/7c/tirewear_fixture.esm`, byte for byte, from national tables rather than from the run's own copies of them.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "tw_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-tirewear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020. The scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "tw_runspecmonth": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-tirewear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecmonth.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecmonth"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, monthID 8.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "tw_runspechour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-tirewear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspechour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspechour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, hourID 7. Six in the RunSpec XML, seven here: the XML's @key is a 0-based index into the sorted hour list (docs/mixed-onroad.md 0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "tw_runspecday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-tirewear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecday.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, dayID 5 (weekday). The second factor of the activity axis and of the output axis, and its extent is one in this run: `<day id=\"5\">` selects one day type where the earlier `<day key=\"5\">` was an out-of-range INDEX and fell back to both (moves.rs PR #55).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "tw_runspecsourcetype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-tirewear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecsourcetype.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecsourcetype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, sourceTypeID 21.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "tw_runspecroadtype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-tirewear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecroadtype.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecroadtype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, roadTypeID 4. J27: this is the join that suppresses every process-2 row, because start exhaust lives on the off-network road type 1 and the RunSpec does not select it (§0.2).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "tw_runspecsourcefueltype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-tirewear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecsourcefueltype.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecsourcefueltype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "cohorts"
        ],
        "note": "4 rows: gasoline, diesel, E85 and electricity. The second factor of the cohort candidate grid.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "tw_movesoutput": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-tirewear/tables/db__out_process_tirewear__movesoutput.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "emissionQuant"
        ]
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "oracle",
          "expected-output"
        ],
        "note": "The 750-row expected output -- 250 rows each for pollutants 91, 107 and 117, shipped in the same snapshot so no canonical MOVES, MariaDB or JVM is needed to develop against it. DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING -- reading it would transcribe the answer and its extent would transcribe the answer's shape. compare-output.py reads it directly under tolerance.toml.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "tw_runspecpollutantprocess": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-tirewear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecpollutantprocess.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecpollutantprocess"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "3 rows: 9101 (Total Energy x Running Exhaust), 10710 (PM10 Tirewear, chained) and 11710 (PM2.5 Tirewear x Tirewear). This relation is the fixture's SECOND output-block axis and the only place the run's pollutant/process scope is written down -- it comes from here and never from the RunSpec XML. It is also what `pp_W` is keyed by: the PROCESS half of each id decides which of the two operating-mode generators wrote its weights.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "tw_runspecchainedto": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-tirewear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecchainedto.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecchainedto"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "1 row: 10710 <- 11710. MOVES's own statement that PM10 Tirewear is a CHAINED pollutant, computed by scaling its PM2.5 sibling rather than from a rate of its own (PM10BrakeTireCalculator). The document reads the chain from here rather than writing `107 = ratio x 117`.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "tw_runspeccounty": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-tirewear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspeccounty.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspeccounty"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, countyID 26161. The runspec selection this catalogue did not have to carry while `link` arrived pre-selected. It changes nothing here -- the snapshot's `link` is the one row this joins to -- and it is what makes the same logic readable against a national Link table.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "ProcessTirewear": {
      "ref": "../../moves-onroad.esm"
    }
  }
